  "reasons": {
    "dead|span.brief-index": "The 01/02/03 index of a brief item, in a two-column row whose second column is the sentence itself (184x43 measured at 1241px). The index is 24px wide because a number is 24px wide; the row is full of text.",
    "dead|span.lang-badge.insights-bar-en": "A 15px language tag beside the insight sentence it labels. That sentence is 169x168 and fills the row. A tag is short because a tag is short.",
    "dead|div.gp-totals": "The totals line of a two-part ground-pulse lane header. The lane kicker beside it is 50x89 and fills the row; the totals are one line that has nothing else to say.",
    "dead|div#mapKicker": "The map's title line, in the map panel header. The tall thing in that row is the map panel below it, not empty space: re-measured with the disclosure open, the title-wrap is 38px and the kicker fills it. The 302px band only exists while the panel is closed.",
    "dead|div.hg-level": "The current gauge reading in a three-column haze row whose first column is the gauge drawing at 142x111. The drawing fills the row.",
    "dead|div.hg-band": "The severity band label in the same three-column haze row — one word beside the gauge drawing that gives the band its meaning.",
    "clip|div.metric-label": "Keep the simultaneous rain, warning, air, particulate, heat and airport overview above the working map. At narrow desktop widths some headings abbreviate; each adjoining normal-flow Why this action exposes the full metric name, value, context and provenance to keyboard and touch readers. Font size is not reduced. This does not exempt a control from covering any reading or freshness text.",
    "clip|div.metric-context": "Truncation here is a measured trade, not an oversight. The context is DATA — 'NREB official · Moderate · 21 October 2026, Wednesday 15:45' — and a KPI tile is a fixed cell of a six-across band (90px at 1041px), so the qualifier does not fit on one line. It was changed to a two-line wrap on 22 Oct and reverted the same day: tests/anti-slop.test.mjs records the band regrowing to 118px, which took 118px off the map. The map is the product, so the qualifier truncates — and carries its full text in a title attribute, so hover recovers it.",
    "clip|span.src-fresh": "Climate provenance combines observation age with baked/browser tier; at the narrowest desktop tiles that supplemental line abbreviates while the metric remains visible. Full age and tier are available through the adjoining keyboard/touch Why this action and title. NREB uses a compact observation-age caption, never retrieval age: its clipping and any evidence-control/glyph overlap are independently rejected by the portable gate, regardless of this reason.",
    "clip|div.metric-source": "The provenance row is not on screen at rest: opacity:0, max-height:0, revealed on hover inside a 30px box. At the narrowest tile (90px at 1041px) the name and its timestamp need two lines, so the row's scroll width exceeds its box. Nothing is hidden from a reader because nothing is shown until they ask for it.",
    "clip|span.news-digest-title": "A news headline under a deliberate two-line clamp (reading.css, same clamp the ground pulse uses). A headline can be longer than two lines of a 254-340px rail; the clamp keeps the map's rail from growing, and the full headline is in the title attribute so hover recovers it. Truncation here is chosen and recoverable, not loss."
  },
